1
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,440
(18+ viewers only)

2
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,960
(18+ viewers only
(May contain disturbing content)

3
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,120
(Contains violence, sex,
and strong language)

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,720
(This series is a work of fiction and is not related to any actual person, place, organization, or event.)

5
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,120
(During the production process, AI technology was used in certain scenes to support on-set safety,)

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,000
(as well as to enhance the quality and realism of the visual presentation.)

7
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:35,680
Panin confirms the tattoo
is in the same spot as Tee's.

8
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,640
We need stronger evidence.

9
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:42,880
This alone

10
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:44,480
doesn't prove it's Tee.

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Besides the tattoo,

12
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,160
is there anything else
that can identify him?

13
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:52,800
Dental records can also
confirm his identity.

14
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,520
Dr. Ji,

15
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,120
I'll leave this to you.

16
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,720
The DNA results
from the police blood test,

17
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:15,800
are they back yet?

18
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,080
Well...

19
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,800
The results are back, but...

20
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,280
we still can't extract the DNA.

21
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,880
What we saw yesterday

22
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,640
wasn't something
a normal person could do.

23
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,240
Do you believe the stories about Nour?

24
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,280
How much do you know about Nour?

25
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,920
Not much more than you do.

26
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,720
As for whether I believe
Nour really exists...

27
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,000
I didn't at first.

28
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,680
Not until I saw it myself.

29
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:03,560
Okay.

30
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,600
I'm the exact opposite.

31
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:06,280
Because

32
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,360
I don't believe the stories about Nour.

33
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,160
Nin.

34
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,120
Are you okay?

35
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,840
So, was that really Tee?

36
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,280
I'm not sure either.

37
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,560
We'll know once they confirm it.

38
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:52,600
Hey.

39
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,240
Don't overthink it.

40
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,840
Maybe it isn't Tee at all.

41
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,720
Can you give me a minute?

42
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,280
I want to be alone.

43
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,400
(Police Station)

44
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,680
Your wound is healing well.

45
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:55,160
Maybe I found a really good doctor.

46
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,040
Easy.

47
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,680
It's still bruised.

48
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,640
If the victim really is Tee,

49
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:12,680
then the Nour at the station
must've been someone else.

50
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:17,960
But we still don't have enough
proof that the body is Tee's.

51
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:20,600
I know.

52
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,640
But if it really is Tee,

53
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:27,760
do you think that Nour killed him?

54
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,640
If I'm right,

55
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,240
then fire can kill Nour.

56
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,240
It...

57
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,520
doesn't die that easily.

58
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,640
What do you mean?

59
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,800
Sergeant Phong.

60
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,480
(Inspector, where are you right now?)

61
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:51,920
How did you get my contact info?

62
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,800
Didn't I tell you

63
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,800
I'd add you to the group chat?

64
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,400
What did Phong say?

65
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,080
Wait, Inspector.

66
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,400
Ms. Prae, are you
the doctor on call, or...?

67
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:21,320
I'm a medical technology
student interning here.

68
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,680
Like I said before,

69
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:26,320
I forgot something here
and came back for it.

70
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:28,600
But as I was heading home,

71
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,000
I suddenly blacked out.

72
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:32,360
I don't remember anything after.

73
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,640
The Medical Technology Department
is on the other side.

74
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,960
It's pretty far from
the Forensic Medicine Department.

75
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,800
There must be cameras there.

76
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,440
Do you remember where you woke up?

77
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,280
Can you tell us

78
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,720
where you woke up?

79
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,760
I woke up in a car trunk.

80
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:55,240
My hands and feet were tied.

81
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,160
My mouth was taped shut.

82
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:58,400
So I...

83
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:02,000
struggled as hard as I could
to get free.

84
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:03,920
I kicked the trunk open and escaped.

85
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,840
Do you remember

86
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:09,800
what the attacker looked like?

87
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:11,760
No.

88
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,880
He attacked me from behind.

89
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,360
I don't remember anything after.

90
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,080
Your left arm.

91
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,240
How did you hurt it?

92
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,000
This?

93
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,040
I was cooking for Tee

94
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,920
and accidentally burned myself.

95
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:29,920
But...

96
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,960
ever since I moved here,

97
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,480
I haven't been able to reach Tee.

98
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,200
Can you help me reach him?

99
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,280
He's my boyfriend.

100
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:45,000
Do you or your boyfriend
have any enemies?

101
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:47,480
No.

102
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,200
Could it be that...

103
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,920
I can't reach him

104
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,320
because he was kidnapped too?

105
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:57,680
Ms. Prae.

106
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:02,280
We found a body that may be Tee's.

107
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,440
If you know anything else

108
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:06,520
or remember something,

109
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,520
contact us right away.

110
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,080
This way.

111
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,560
(Criminal Investigation Division)

112
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,920
When you found the body,

113
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,280
did you see a phone

114
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,040
or any personal belongings?

115
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,320
Why would you ask that?

116
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,040
Because...

117
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:49,200
if you found anything else,

118
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,040
I'm his girlfriend.

119
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:54,360
I might know if it belonged to Tee.

120
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,760
We'll contact you
if we find more evidence.

121
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,360
Thank you.

122
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,360
Why did you...?

123
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,480
I don't trust her.

124
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:22,120
I'll get his dental records
to identify the body.

125
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,080
That should be more reliable.

126
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,040
Thanks.

127
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:26,920
No problem.

128
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:28,920
Whatever you want, Inspector,

129
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,520
it's yours.

130
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,360
Quit joking around.

131
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,160
I'm serious.

132
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,560
Go get the evidence.

133
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,000
And fix your clothes.

134
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:47,680
Yes, sir.

135
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,480
This patient has been here
several times before.

136
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:07,600
You can see his wisdom tooth
was removed on this side.

137
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:12,000
Please provide his records
to the police.

138
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:13,960
No problem.

139
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:17,280
Has anyone told you you're cute?

140
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,320
Once or twice.

141
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,000
Afterward,

142
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:27,400
I'll send them to Forensics
for comparison.

143
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,440
Tomorrow's Valentine's Day.

144
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,040
Care to join me for a meal?

145
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,640
Well...

146
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:39,920
I'm already seeing someone.

147
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:41,480
But thank you.

148
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:52,040
The X-ray shows tooth 38 is missing.

149
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,000
The body's condition
is similar to Somying's.

150
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:56,720
Right.

151
00:10:57,640 --> 00:10:59,200
The internal burns
are worse than the external ones.

152
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:02,800
But it's too early to tell
if they're the same type of case.

153
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:06,360
We can't draw conclusions
just because the bodies look alike.

154
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:14,320
By the way...

155
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:17,920
Are you spending

156
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:20,240
Valentine's Day in
the autopsy room again?

157
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:21,520
Why?

158
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:24,120
Spending it with someone special?

159
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,560
No, Doctor.

160
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:27,680
It's just...

161
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:32,120
unlike you, I don't have an inspector.

162
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,040
Getting cheeky, aren't you?

163
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,920
Was I really that bad?

164
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,240
Excuse me.

165
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:41,360
Chita.

166
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,240
Are you done already?

167
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:44,480
Yes.

168
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,440
It's pretty late,

169
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,960
but the lights were still on,
so I came to turn them off.

170
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:54,640
No need.

171
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,000
I'll do it.

172
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,320
You can go.

173
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,120
I'll leave it to you.

174
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,240
Let's go, Chita.

175
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,000
Oh, right.

176
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,600
Your fever's gone, right?

177
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:14,840
Yes.

178
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,240
Thank you so much, Dr. Ji.

179
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,120
What's wrong?

180
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:25,840
Well...

181
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,920
Tomorrow's Valentine's Day.

182
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,520
Do you have any plans?

183
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,200
Not yet.

184
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:36,760
But I'm planning

185
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,560
to help Dr. Ken.

186
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,920
Tee's case has stalled.
Maybe we can find more evidence.

187
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:46,760
Doctor.

188
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,360
I want to ask you something.

189
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:49,560
Go ahead.

190
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:52,560
When we kissed that day...

191
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:56,720
did it...

192
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,760
mean anything to you?

193
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:21,360
Well...

194
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:23,480
I...

195
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:26,280
Chita.

196
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,760
I remember your interview.

197
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,640
Didn't you say
you weren't afraid of ghosts?

198
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:33,760
I'm not.

199
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:35,720
Well...

200
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,960
we should head home.

201
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,280
Too many strange things
have been happening.

202
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,080
You can go first.

203
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,760
I'll turn off the lights.

204
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,280
It's okay.

205
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,680
I'll stay with you.

206
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,320
Suit yourself.

207
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:55,600
If you're scared,

208
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:57,720
hold me tight.

209
00:13:58,680 --> 00:13:59,320
I'm not scared.

210
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:28,520
The victim's skin was badly damaged.

211
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,880
Almost no marks remain,

212
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:34,600
except the tattoo on his left chest.

213
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:56,680
Hey.

214
00:14:58,920 --> 00:14:59,480
What are you doing?

215
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,440
Doesn't anything scare you?

216
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,320
I'm working.

217
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:05,800
Move.

218
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,360
I got you coffee.

219
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:11,240
I figured you hadn't eaten.

220
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:12,640
Thanks.

221
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,360
But I'm not hungry yet.

222
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,320
I already got it. Just take it.

223
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,600
You can drink it later.

224
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:29,200
And this.

225
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,760
A copy of Tee's dental X-ray.

226
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:37,440
Consider it your Valentine's gift.

227
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:45,360
Then where's

228
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,080
my gift?

229
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:56,960
There isn't one.

230
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,400
This is a hospital.

231
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:01,920
Show some respect.

232
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,200
Inspector.

233
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:04,840
You're not romantic at all.

234
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,120
How can you be romantic
with a corpse right there?

235
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,280
Hmm.

236
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,000
I'd say

237
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:16,240
it's about

238
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,240
as romantic as kissing at the station.

239
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,520
Your hands are freezing.

240
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,960
And your pulse is irregular.

241
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:48,680
This came with it.

242
00:16:50,040 --> 00:16:50,440
Well?

243
00:16:51,680 --> 00:16:52,360
Cute, just like me.

244
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,640
You like it, don't you?

245
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,960
Don't let me catch you hanging it up.

246
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,640
According to Tee's dental records,

247
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,000
he had a root canal,

248
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,080
a post and crown,

249
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,600
and had his lower-left
wisdom tooth removed.

250
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,120
That means...

251
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,640
it's a perfect match.

252
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,080
So the body really is Tee.

253
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:53,280
(Jiratikarn Nantawanchai)

254
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:10,080
(Happy Valentine's Day, Doctor.
Thanks for taking care of me.)

255
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,760
Happy Valentine's Day.

256
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,560
Happy Valentine's Day, Dr. Ji.

257
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:26,000
- That department moved fast.
- There's the first one.

258
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:28,520
- Thanks.
- First? The wall's filling up.

259
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:30,800
Any luck this Valentine's Day?

260
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:32,480
Calm down. The doctor has standards.

261
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,200
Sis.

262
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,160
- Yeah?
- Here. Put this up.

263
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:37,480
Thanks.

264
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:39,600
You've worked with him for so long.

265
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:40,800
Why not ask him out?

266
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:42,600
- That's bold.
- Thanks.

267
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,440
- Put it up, Doctor.
- Doctor.

268
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,800
There's an emergency
in the Forensic Lab.

269
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,440
This way.

270
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:48,800
Another emergency?

271
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:50,840
I'll get going.
Please put it in my office.

272
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:54,240
- Sure. Go on.
- Thanks. Sorry.

273
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:58,680
386, get to work.
You two slack off all day.

274
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,760
We don't.

275
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:01,320
Chita.

276
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,280
Chita.

277
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,120
Wait.

278
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,760
What is it?

279
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:09,280
I'm sorry.

280
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,520
I interrupted you earlier.

281
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:15,320
Don't apologize, Chita.
You actually saved me.

282
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:18,640
I never knew

283
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:21,960
you had so many admirers.

284
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:28,440
So...

285
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:33,360
is there someone you like?

286
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:36,240
Well...

287
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,720
Am I interrupting?

288
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:42,720
Well...

289
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:44,600
It's okay.

290
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:45,080
Actually,

291
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:45,840
I...

292
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,600
wanted to ask about the case.

293
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,840
You saw the evidence I sent, right?

294
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:50,720
I did.

295
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,320
The dental findings match.

296
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:53,240
So...

297
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:54,920
this really is Tee.

298
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,520
I think so too.

299
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:58,920
Now we need to find out

300
00:19:59,160 --> 00:19:59,960
who killed Tee

301
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,400
and what we've missed.

302
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,840
First, we need to find his next of kin.

303
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,200
I already checked his background.

304
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,120
Tee's parents both died.

305
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:11,080
He had no siblings
or other known relatives.

306
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,080
There was only one name.

307
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,000
Excuse me.

308
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,160
You holding up?

309
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:56,920
It really is Tee.

310
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:00,840
How did this happen to him?

311
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,440
He was murdered.

312
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,200
Who did it?

313
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,280
We don't know yet.

314
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:13,240
We tested his blood,

315
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,640
body chemistry,

316
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,520
the soot in his lungs,

317
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,880
and his skeletal structure.

318
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:21,920
But the body was badly burned,

319
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:25,920
so there wasn't any useful
evidence left.

320
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:36,840
We may ask you to return
for more questions.

321
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,280
I'll cooperate.

322
00:21:40,240 --> 00:21:41,680
I just want the killer caught.

323
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,920
Before you were kidnapped,

324
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,240
did anything strange happen to Tee?

325
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,800
Tee and I planned to meet.

326
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,440
But once I got to Nakhon Sawan,

327
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,440
I couldn't reach him at all.

328
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:00,520
I thought he was just busy with exams.

329
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,920
I never imagined this would happen.

330
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:35,880
I'll...

331
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:38,080
arrange Tee's funeral.

332
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,640
Thanks for bringing me here.

333
00:22:56,360 --> 00:22:57,360
Anytime, Inspector.

334
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,040
A Valentine's gift.

335
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,040
For you.

336
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:23,240
So this is the evidence
I was looking for in your car.

337
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:25,800
Make a copy, then return it.

338
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:27,560
And don't lose it.

339
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:28,640
Understood?

340
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:31,280
Got it.

341
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,240
I won't let you down.

342
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:39,680
Give me your hand.

343
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:43,640
Give me your hand.

344
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:07,880
Thanks.

345
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,520
Drive safe, Inspector.

346
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:50,480
Happy Valentine's Day, Doctor.

347
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:52,720
Thank you

348
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,240
for taking care of me.

349
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:57,440
Nin, give me that.

350
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:01,680
Do forensic doctors
care for patients too?

351
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:02,960
Or did someone give you this?

352
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:05,960
Stop going through my stuff.
Don't you have class?

353
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:08,400
Class is over.

354
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:10,440
Can you go home now?

355
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:12,400
Go home and see Mom too.

356
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:14,440
If you don't want it, I do.

357
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,160
No.

358
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,600
If that's all you came for,
can't you just call next time?

359
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:20,720
You never pick up.

360
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,200
I just heard you're seeing someone new.

361
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:26,080
Choose more carefully this time.

362
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:28,160
Not like the last one.

363
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:32,080
Did you finish the notes I asked for?

364
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:35,960
If you paid attention,
you could make your own.

365
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:39,400
Fine. That's the best I can do.

366
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,480
How are you getting home?

367
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:47,920
I'll go on my own.

368
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:50,760
I'm taking this.

369
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:18,840
Hey.

370
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:20,840
Did I scare you?

371
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:24,240
What's wrong?

372
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,000
You look miserable.

373
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:29,360
I'm frustrated.

374
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:31,320
I really don't get my brother.

375
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:33,400
What's bothering you?

376
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:34,840
Did you two fight?

377
00:26:35,320 --> 00:26:35,640
Yeah.

378
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:39,440
I just don't want him dating anyone.

379
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:42,440
You know what happened
in his last relationship.

380
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:44,120
Come here.

381
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:44,960
What?

382
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:45,800
You know,

383
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:47,800
your brother's a catch.

384
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:51,720
It's no surprise people hit on him.

385
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,560
I'm cute too, okay?

386
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,360
How come no one hits on me?

387
00:26:58,720 --> 00:27:00,040
Fine. You're very cute.

388
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:08,000
Here.

389
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:10,080
I've got some chocolate for you.

390
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:11,400
Want a bite?

391
00:27:13,120 --> 00:27:14,560
A girl gave it to you. Why not keep it?

392
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:16,080
Why are you giving it to me?

393
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,200
I don't like her anyway.

394
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:19,720
So what?

395
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:21,320
Do you want it or not?

396
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:22,040
Tsk.

397
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:23,400
Fine. I do.

398
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:24,840
Seriously.

399
00:27:25,320 --> 00:27:26,240
Playing it cool.

400
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:27,240
I'll get you one.

401
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:29,800
What color? Red? No.

402
00:27:30,560 --> 00:27:31,640
Pink?

403
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:32,800
No.

404
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:34,120
Blue, then.

405
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:35,240
Here.

406
00:27:36,680 --> 00:27:37,280
You know my favorite color?

407
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:37,800
Tsk.

408
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:40,880
They're all the same.
None are sweeter than me.

409
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:42,320
I'm the sweetest.

410
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:44,520
Nonsense.

411
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:48,240
I'm kidding. Can't I even joke?

412
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:50,840
I was about to go home,

413
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,400
but you texted, so I stayed.

414
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:56,040
Don't you feel lucky

415
00:27:56,520 --> 00:27:57,040
to have a friend like me?

416
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,760
Who else would love you as much as I do?

417
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,680
Want a photo?

418
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:05,560
You mean here?

419
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:06,600
Sure.

420
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:07,960
Come on.

421
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:20,720
Done?

422
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:21,960
Let me see.

423
00:28:22,280 --> 00:28:22,760
Wait.

424
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:24,080
Hey, I want to see it too.

425
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:25,800
Let me see.

426
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:27,200
Sit down first.

427
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:40,320
(Ken: The police station thing.)

428
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:42,480
(No report to his superiors yet, right?)

429
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:43,560
Not yet.

430
00:28:46,280 --> 00:28:46,600
Yes.

431
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:48,680
But why keep it secret?

432
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:54,400
(Ken: The killer may be closer
than we think. Keep it quiet.)

433
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:55,480
Yes. Got it.

434
00:28:56,520 --> 00:28:57,080
Phong.

435
00:28:57,360 --> 00:28:58,120
Talk later.

436
00:28:59,480 --> 00:28:59,800
Okay.

437
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:01,440
How's your wound?

438
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:02,560
Still hurt?

439
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:03,600
It's much better.

440
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,840
I was scared I'd catch
the Nour virus.

441
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:08,840
You're lucky to be alive.

442
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:12,360
Right.

443
00:29:13,680 --> 00:29:14,680
Dr. Jirat sent this.

444
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:17,360
Tee's teeth match
the bite on Mint's neck.

445
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:19,680
Nour really is everywhere.

446
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:23,800
We can close Mint's case.

447
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:25,920
Then do you think

448
00:29:26,600 --> 00:29:28,880
Tee was the Nour
behind all those killings?

449
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:32,120
I almost thought so.

450
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:34,520
But Tee's dead now.

451
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,800
That means there's more than one Nour.

452
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,160
And I have a feeling

453
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:44,760
the real killer behind all this

454
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:46,640
is that Nour.

455
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:50,320
A few days ago,

456
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:51,800
I looked into Prae.

457
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:56,440
She did go back to get something,

458
00:29:56,800 --> 00:30:00,560
but after that,
she never appeared on camera.

459
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:03,920
The camera timestamps
match Prae's statement.

460
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:06,680
Based on the evidence we have,

461
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:07,880
we can't prove she's lying.

462
00:30:13,120 --> 00:30:15,760
But we can't rule her out
as a suspect either.

463
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:17,920
Ugh.

464
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:18,840
My head hurts.

465
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:21,640
Why is this case so complicated?

466
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:22,880
Cases like this

467
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,440
take time.

468
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:02,720
(Trin Prayonsin
Jul. 7, 2003-Feb. 9, 2026)

469
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:40,120
Chita.

470
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:41,560
Did you go home already?

471
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,880
Why didn't you tell me?

472
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,240
This isn't like you.

473
00:31:47,360 --> 00:31:48,240
Are you okay?

474
00:31:53,760 --> 00:31:54,160
All right.

475
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:55,720
I'll finish up here.

476
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:56,680
I'll call you later.

477
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:06,200
Inspector.

478
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:10,560
You look troubled.

479
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:12,880
If something's wrong,

480
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:14,720
you can talk to me.

481
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:19,080
You look

482
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:20,360
more stressed than I do.

483
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:22,520
Can't blame you, though.

484
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:24,480
The killer's already dead.

485
00:32:25,040 --> 00:32:26,640
This case won't be easy to close.

486
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:29,480
But I think

487
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:30,880
work is easier to handle

488
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:33,760
than relationships.

489
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:35,000
Don't you think?

490
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:38,200
What about you and Ken?

491
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:39,160
How's that going?

492
00:32:39,720 --> 00:32:41,320
You've worked together a while.

493
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:43,360
Pretty well.

494
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,600
I think Inspector Ken and I

495
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:48,440
work really well together.

496
00:32:49,520 --> 00:32:50,920
Someone like Ken

497
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:53,600
can actually work well
with someone else?

498
00:32:58,560 --> 00:32:59,680
Then again...

499
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,600
maybe if it's you.

500
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:05,000
Speaking of which,

501
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:06,280
you and Chita...

502
00:33:06,520 --> 00:33:07,400
what's going on there?

503
00:33:09,120 --> 00:33:10,800
I can kind of tell.

504
00:33:14,040 --> 00:33:15,160
I think...

505
00:33:16,560 --> 00:33:17,920
if you like someone,

506
00:33:18,680 --> 00:33:19,760
you should tell them.

507
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:21,920
Life

508
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:24,520
is shorter than we think.

509
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:20,480
I'm sorry for your loss.

510
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:23,000
Thank you.

511
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:25,800
You must be devastated.

512
00:34:26,640 --> 00:34:28,240
You probably planned a future together.

513
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:31,640
And you never thought a Nour could die.

514
00:34:36,680 --> 00:34:37,800
Why do you make it sound

515
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,840
like I knew Tee was a Nour?

516
00:34:40,680 --> 00:34:42,320
Isn't that pretty likely?

517
00:34:43,680 --> 00:34:44,800
If you truly love someone,

518
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:46,800
you'd do anything

519
00:34:47,640 --> 00:34:49,280
to stay with them longer.

520
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:52,560
Even become a Nour yourself

521
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:55,040
so you can be together forever.

522
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:56,560
Right?

523
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:01,560
Yes.

524
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:03,960
I'm his girlfriend.

525
00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:06,880
Of course I wanted to stay with him.

526
00:35:07,600 --> 00:35:09,240
But don't you think

527
00:35:09,880 --> 00:35:12,400
calling me a Nour is going too far?

528
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,800
Losing him already hurts enough.

529
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:18,080
Or are you saying this

530
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:21,520
because you've never lost
someone you loved?

531
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:31,960
Hey, careful.

532
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:36,200
When this case is over,

533
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:38,000
I want you to try doing something else.

534
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:42,640
You still won't let this go?

535
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:43,680
You...

536
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:44,960
Are you okay?

537
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:55,600
Where have you been?

538
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:56,840
Are you okay?

539
00:35:58,280 --> 00:35:59,400
I just needed to think.

540
00:36:01,520 --> 00:36:02,840
Don't push yourself too hard.

541
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:05,600
No matter what,
we'll find the real killer.

542
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:08,400
No matter the danger

543
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:09,960
or the cost,

544
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:11,680
I'm not afraid.

545
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:17,280
I'll catch whoever killed
my father and the others.

546
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:33,880
Doctor, are you okay?

547
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:38,120
I'm just thinking.

548
00:36:38,560 --> 00:36:39,640
I'm fine.

549
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:44,120
It looks like more than that.

550
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:50,120
Actually...

551
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:51,960
I did something

552
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:55,600
and I don't know if it was right.

553
00:36:58,520 --> 00:36:59,080
Hmm.

554
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,360
I've never

555
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:03,520
seen you like this either.

556
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:08,760
Forget it.

557
00:37:09,840 --> 00:37:10,960
I've made my decision.

558
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,080
It's probably for the best.

559
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:14,800
Actually...

560
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:17,400
there's something

561
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:19,480
I can't decide either.

562
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:25,320
Let's get to work.

563
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:26,280
Come on.

564
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:27,520
Okay.

565
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:40,440
Doctor.

566
00:37:41,040 --> 00:37:42,320
I'll be right back.

567
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:53,280
Chita.

568
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:56,920
If you don't feel anything for me,

569
00:37:58,960 --> 00:38:00,520
but still treat me this way,

570
00:38:01,880 --> 00:38:03,120
that's really cruel.

571
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:08,080
I think...

572
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:10,120
if you like someone,

573
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:12,200
you should tell them.

574
00:38:13,200 --> 00:38:14,320
Life

575
00:38:15,400 --> 00:38:16,880
is shorter than we think.

576
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:26,160
Chita, come here.

577
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:36,040
I'm sorry.

578
00:38:36,720 --> 00:38:37,960
I didn't get you

579
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:39,520
a Valentine's gift.

580
00:38:46,120 --> 00:38:48,200
Cook for me again sometime.

581
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:53,240
Only for me.

582
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:57,800
As for this note...

583
00:38:58,240 --> 00:39:00,000
(Happy Valentine's Day, Doctor.
Thanks for taking care of me.)

584
00:39:00,640 --> 00:39:01,960
I'm keeping it.

585
00:39:08,600 --> 00:39:09,240
Doctor.

586
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,400
About that day...

587
00:39:15,080 --> 00:39:16,880
how could I feel nothing?

588
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:20,120
Not after you kissed me like that.

589
00:39:30,160 --> 00:39:34,800
♪In a love that can never be real♪

590
00:39:37,120 --> 00:39:41,680
♪You gaze in my soul
and share what I feel♪

591
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:48,880
♪Gray days all fade away, I'm healed♪

592
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:49,440
Doctor.

593
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:52,240
This is a hospital.

594
00:39:52,280 --> 00:39:56,400
♪My dull world starts to glow and shine♪

595
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,600
Isn't this exciting?

596
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:04,520
♪Bound by fate we cannot break
Silent thoughts we both share♪

597
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:10,920
♪Found a light no dark can shake♪

598
00:40:12,080 --> 00:40:17,920
♪We make a wish toward rainbow's end♪

599
00:40:19,600 --> 00:40:24,720
♪Chase the dream beyond the bend♪

600
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:33,800
♪Though this hope can never
reach the ground♪

601
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:38,240
♪You painted hills in my barren land♪

602
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:48,480
(Pathology Room)

603
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:00,920
Hello, sir.

604
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:03,520
Yes.

605
00:41:03,600 --> 00:41:09,200
(It's a shame the killer
you were after died.)

606
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:10,480
Thank you, sir.

607
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:19,760
(As of today, you're off
all arson cases.)

608
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:21,080
Suspend everything?

609
00:41:21,240 --> 00:41:22,480
Wait. What do you mean?

610
00:41:22,520 --> 00:41:25,720
(Enough. You did well,
but it's no longer your responsibility.)

611
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:30,120
(Report back to Bangkok.
I've signed your transfer order.)

612
00:41:31,160 --> 00:41:32,320
Inspector.

613
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:33,520
Inspector.

614
00:41:36,720 --> 00:41:37,840
Congratulations.

615
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,920
The case is officially closed.

616
00:41:42,080 --> 00:41:42,640
Tangme.

617
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:43,440
Phong.

618
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:46,920
I've been ordered back to headquarters.

619
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:47,720
What?

620
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:48,440
How?

621
00:41:48,960 --> 00:41:49,680
A new transfer order?

622
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:50,280
Why?

623
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,360
I don't know.

624
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:56,400
I don't understand.

625
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,320
I followed every procedure.

626
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:01,080
And the evidence I found

627
00:42:01,520 --> 00:42:03,480
helped clarify the case.

628
00:42:05,760 --> 00:42:07,080
So I can't help wondering

629
00:42:08,080 --> 00:42:09,160
if there's more

630
00:42:11,360 --> 00:42:12,960
to this transfer.

631
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:15,360
I don't know.

632
00:42:16,920 --> 00:42:18,680
I had no idea about the transfer.

633
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:20,400
Who do you think is behind it?

634
00:42:56,200 --> 00:43:00,640
(Police Station)

635
00:43:04,320 --> 00:43:05,000
Hey, you.

636
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:06,160
Where are you going?

637
00:43:10,040 --> 00:43:10,680
Hey.

638
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:13,040
We need to talk.

639
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:20,640
(Police Station)

640
00:44:05,520 --> 00:44:05,960
What?

641
00:44:06,680 --> 00:44:08,080
You had me transferred, didn't you?

642
00:44:08,480 --> 00:44:09,520
Why did you do it?

643
00:44:10,800 --> 00:44:11,600
Why won't you say anything?

644
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:12,800
Answer me.

645
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:14,800
I just told you.

646
00:44:24,200 --> 00:44:25,480
It's for the best.

647
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:27,360
The best?

648
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:29,080
Like heck it is.

649
00:44:29,560 --> 00:44:31,840
I was stupid to trust you.

650
00:44:33,200 --> 00:44:34,560
Was messing with my feelings

651
00:44:34,880 --> 00:44:36,080
fun for you?

652
00:44:38,840 --> 00:44:40,880
Did you ever think about how I'd feel?

653
00:44:42,720 --> 00:44:43,640
All this time,

654
00:44:45,400 --> 00:44:47,280
I thought you trusted me.

655
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:50,320
I thought we trusted each other.

656
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:57,520
I don't even like

657
00:44:58,320 --> 00:44:59,440
this awful place that much.

658
00:45:00,520 --> 00:45:02,120
But there are two reasons

659
00:45:03,160 --> 00:45:04,760
that keep me here.

660
00:45:06,200 --> 00:45:07,000
The first

661
00:45:07,840 --> 00:45:09,000
is finding the killer.

662
00:45:10,240 --> 00:45:11,120
The second

663
00:45:11,840 --> 00:45:12,760
is you.

664
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:17,000
So...

665
00:45:18,440 --> 00:45:19,720
can I stay here?

666
00:45:21,680 --> 00:45:22,880
I don't care what role I have.

667
00:45:27,120 --> 00:45:28,520
Didn't you say at the bar

668
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:30,800
that we're friends?

669
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:33,920
I don't have to stay a cop.

670
00:45:36,360 --> 00:45:37,760
Just let me stay here,

671
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:40,120
by your side.

672
00:45:46,000 --> 00:45:46,680
After all this time,

673
00:45:46,720 --> 00:45:47,520
I know

674
00:45:49,360 --> 00:45:50,800
you feel it too, right?

675
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:20,480
This came with it.

676
00:46:25,800 --> 00:46:26,760
You like it, don't you?

677
00:46:47,400 --> 00:46:49,080
I don't feel that way about you.

678
00:46:52,920 --> 00:46:53,760
You're lying.

679
00:46:57,520 --> 00:46:58,480
Get out.

680
00:47:00,880 --> 00:47:02,880
You're just afraid
you'll like me even more.

681
00:47:05,680 --> 00:47:06,480
I'm right, aren't I?

682
00:47:13,640 --> 00:47:14,840
Even if that's true,

683
00:47:15,960 --> 00:47:16,800
to me,

684
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:19,880
work and feelings are separate.

685
00:47:20,960 --> 00:47:22,080
Get out.

686
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,000
What are you doing?

687
00:48:00,880 --> 00:48:01,600
I'm not leaving.

688
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,880
Not until you stop pretending
you feel nothing for me.

689
00:48:15,760 --> 00:48:17,800
See? You do feel something.

